
Narrator: November 1st, 2002. Lewisburg, Pennsylvania. Halloween is over, and Costume Cove has survived another year.

Narrator: You've spent months making costumes by hand. Every stitch, every seam, every questionable fashion decision. And now, finally, it's time to count your profits.

Narrator: But running a business isn't just about money. Your reputation matters, too. Some customers deserve their money back. Others deserve a firm no.

Narrator: Inspect the costumes, question the customers, and make the right calls. Then lock up and enjoy some well-earned peace and quiet.

Narrator: What could possibly go wrong?

